coder › Done on branch `fix/slugify-accents` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/slugify.ts`: added `.normalize('NFD')` + `.replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, '')` before lowercasing, so accented Latin letters reduce to their base letter (e.g. `è→e`, `û→u`). The existing `[^a-z0-9]+ → '-'` collapse and leading/trailing dash trim were kept unchanged.
- `src/slugify.test.ts`: added 3 tests — `Crème Brûlée → creme-brulee`, dash collapsing/trimming (`'  Hello---World!! ' → 'hello-world'`), and empty/punctuation-only input → `''`. Kept the existing test untouched.

Decisions not in the request: NFD + combining-marks strip handles precomposed and decomposed accents the same way; it does not transliterate non-Latin scripts or ligatures (e.g. `ß`, `ø`, CJK) — those still fall through to the dash rule.

